8	 * @test @b openssl_sha3
9	 * @parblock
10	 * Stress test for SHA-3 (FIPS 202) and SHAKE128 via OpenSSL's EVP digest
11	 * API. SHA-3 is the Keccak-f[1600] sponge permutation: theta (column
12	 * parity), rho (lane rotation), pi (lane transposition), chi (the only
13	 * nonlinear step, an AND-NOT), iota (round-constant XOR). That
14	 * AND-XOR-rotate datapath is orthogonal to SHA-2's mod-2^64 additive
15	 * chains exercised by the companion openssl_sha test, so the two tests
16	 * together cover distinct functional-unit mixes on the crypto pipes.
17	 * SHAKE128 adds the extendable-output-function (XOF) squeeze path with a
18	 * caller-chosen 32-byte output on top of the fixed-length
19	 * sha3-224/256/384/512 digests. The SDC literature synthesis
20	 * (docs/paper/SDC_RESEARCH_SYNTHESIS_CN.md §7.2, priority 2) explicitly
21	 * names SHA-2/3 hashing among the highest-value coverage targets.
22	 * OpenSSL 3.5 runtime-dispatches to its optimized Keccak implementation
23	 * on aarch64. Each iteration copies a randomly chosen golden plaintext
24	 * into an mmap'ed arena at a random offset, recomputes all five digests,
25	 * and byte-compares against golden values calculated once in init
26	 * (copy->compute->verify).
27	 * @endparblock
28	 */
29	
